    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hi, it’s good to meet you. What brings you in today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S004",
      "patient_response": "Hi, yeah, nice to meet you too. Um, so I guess what brings me in is that I'm having a lot of trouble at my job. I work at a meat processing plant, and I keep starting the sanitation steps, or the batch logs, or the end-of-line paperwork, and somehow I just... leave out the last parts. Even when I know my job totally depends on finishing them correctly. \n\nIt’s super strict there. Actually, the safety inspector came by last Tuesday and he was wearing these really weird neon green rubber boots. I remember staring at them thinking they looked like something out of a cartoon, like, who wears neon green on a processing floor? Usually everyone just wears the standard white ones they issue us in the locker room. I had to buy my own gel insoles for mine, though, because standing on that concrete all day is just brutal on your back. My roommate told me I should try yoga for that, since she started going to this studio downtown that does the hot yoga, but... wait, I'm sorry, I completely lost my train of thought. \n\nWhat was I saying? Oh, right, work. Yeah, I just keep leaving my logs and the end of the sanitation stuff unfinished, and I really need to stop doing that before I get fired.",
