    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Did you have this same kind of trouble with attention or finishing things when you were a child?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, definitely. Um, my mom actually still has some of my old report cards from, like, fourth grade? And they always said the same thing—that I was bright but I needed constant reminders to actually finish my classwork or turn in my homework. Which is funny because my mom kept everything. She has this huge plastic bin in her attic filled with all my old school stuff, and some of my brother's too, but mostly mine. She even kept this macaroni art thing I made in kindergarten that smells really weird now. I don't know why she holds onto that stuff, she's trying to downsize right now because she wants to move to Florida. She hates the winters here, which, honestly, I get. The snow just turns into that gross gray slush on the side of the road after two days anyway. \n\nBut, um, yeah, as a kid... I remember I would understand the lessons totally fine, but I'd miss whole chunks of the instructions unless the teacher was, like, standing right next to me.",
