      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Yeah, for sure. Like, my apartment is always a mess because of it. I'll start doing the laundry, right? And then I'll pull out a shirt that I bought back when I was getting my degree—I just finished my bachelor's, actually. But anyway, I got it at this amazing vintage thrift store near campus. The owner had this massive golden retriever that would just sleep right in the middle of the clothing racks, so you literally had to step over him to look at the jackets. I love dogs so much, but my current landlord has a super strict no-pet policy. It's really annoying because I feel like a cat would be great to have around, you know? My roommate really wants a cat too. She was looking at the animal shelter's website the other day and saw this orange tabby that was missing half an ear. It looked like a cute little pirate, and we were trying to figure out if we could sneak it past the landlord, but... wait, sorry. What did you ask me? Oh, right, outside of work. Yeah, I just never actually finish folding the laundry or doing whatever chore I start at home either.",
