    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you often feel anxious or on edge?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, no, not really. I mean, I don't think I feel anxious or on edge very much. Sometimes I get a little stressed when I realize I'm super behind on something, but it's not like a constant anxious feeling, you know? It's more just... being frustrated with myself. \n\nActually, my roommate is the one who gets really anxious. She has this whole morning routine where she has to drink her coffee out of this specific mug that has a little ceramic frog sitting at the bottom of it. She got it at a pottery class we took together last year. I was terrible at it, honestly. My bowl looked like a weird, lopsided lump of clay. But she made this really cool vase, and then she made that frog mug. She says if she doesn't use it, her whole day feels off. I don't really drink coffee, though. It makes my stomach feel weird. I prefer tea, like that chamomile stuff? I found this amazing loose-leaf tea shop downtown, right next to that hot yoga place I mentioned earlier. The owner there is so nice, she always gives me free samples of the new blends. Last time she gave me this peach-mango one that smelled exactly like those gummy rings you get at the gas station. I love those things, especially on road trips. I went on a road trip to Chicago once and... wait, sorry. What were we talking about? \n\nOh, right. No, I don't really feel anxious or on edge. Just mostly distracted, I guess.",
